WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.046
Quality-Oriented Decision Analysis (QODA) is
Jeromy’s lightweight method for making

00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:10.578
architectural decisions informed, shared and
durable, while allowing deliberate revision. A

00:00:10.578 --> 00:00:15.381
technology choice becomes an architectural
decision when it commits a system to

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.840
consequential tradeoffs.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.560
Jeromy’s approach begins by making the context
explicit: whose problem is being solved, what

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:28.060
outcomes matter, which constraints apply, and
what future changes are plausible. A favorite

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.961
product is not a substitute for this definition.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.963
The lecture uses a data-querying example at
Datadog, where diverse kinds of data and

00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:40.984
different storage systems make a unified query
experience difficult. Keep that as the

00:00:40.984 --> 00:00:46.361
motivation for the method, rather than assuming
any historical product comparison remains a

00:00:46.361 --> 00:00:51.678
current recommendation. New worked example used
throughout this unit: a campus information

00:00:51.678 --> 00:00:57.054
service must search course data, export records,
survive worker failures, and integrate new

00:00:57.054 --> 00:00:57.822
data sources.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.733
Alternative A is a tailored service; B is a
shared platform. Before comparing them, record

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:09.274
stakeholders, workload, operating limits, and
non-negotiable constraints. The example’s

00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:14.879
targets and scores are teaching assumptions. Two
teams both want a “good platform.” Have

00:01:14.879 --> 00:01:17.427
they agreed on a decision criterion? No.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.637
They may value latency, incident recovery,
development effort or cost differently. Name

00:01:22.637 --> 00:01:27.773
those priorities and the circumstances in which
each matters before comparing products.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.545
A scenario gives a quality claim a concrete
meaning. The lecture uses context, stimulus and

00:01:33.545 --> 00:01:38.908
response: the conditions in force, the event
that occurs, and the result the system must

00:01:38.908 --> 00:01:42.138
produce. Make the response measurable where
possible.

00:01:42.138 --> 00:01:47.873
A scenario can concern normal execution,
failure, or a development change. Facilitate the

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:53.737
process with stakeholders. The case describes
agreeing on context, inviting participants to

00:01:53.737 --> 00:01:59.666
brainstorm scenarios, refining vague statements,
and then clustering the resulting scenarios

00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:00.955
into a quality tree.

00:02:01.138 --> 00:02:06.312
This bottom-up collection helps expose concerns
that a preselected taxonomy or a product-led

00:02:06.312 --> 00:02:07.324
debate might miss.

00:02:07.324 --> 00:02:13.412
For the campus example, Search means: at 200
requests/second on a specified representative

00:02:13.412 --> 00:02:19.297
dataset, a user issues a search and p95 latency
is at most 250 ms during a defined test

00:02:19.297 --> 00:02:25.249
window. Export means: an authorized user
requests 10,000 records and receives a complete

00:02:25.249 --> 00:02:30.998
export within eight seconds. Specify hardware,
data size and concurrency in an actual

00:02:30.998 --> 00:02:36.815
evaluation. Worker loss means: during a request,
one serving worker terminates and the

00:02:36.815 --> 00:02:39.995
request completes correctly within two seconds.

00:02:39.995 --> 00:02:45.528
New source means: with the platform in
production, the team integrates a new catalog
source

00:02:45.528 --> 00:02:50.758
and produces a tested adapter within three
engineer-days. These are new scenarios, not

00:02:50.758 --> 00:02:56.292
copied lecture questions. Check data correctness
and authorization as well as timing. Agree

00:02:56.292 --> 00:03:01.400
on how evidence will be collected for every
scenario: a load test, a fault-injection

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.110
experiment, a prototype integration, or a
justified analysis.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:10.563
A threshold without a test context is not yet a
reproducible requirement. “The system is

00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:15.955
extensible” is a scenario. True or false? False.
State the change, starting context and

00:03:15.955 --> 00:03:21.470
measurable effort or outcome. For example,
adding a specified source through a documented

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.808
adapter within three engineer-days, with
existing tests still passing.

00:03:25.808 --> 00:03:30.856
A quality tree organizes the meaning of success.
Its upper nodes are qualities such as

00:03:30.856 --> 00:03:35.904
performance, availability and maintainability.
Lower nodes refine those qualities, and

00:03:35.904 --> 00:03:41.304
concrete scenarios sit at the leaves. The
example’s larger tree also illustrates
operational

00:03:41.304 --> 00:03:46.293
and reliability concerns; choose a tree suited
to the system rather than treating one

00:03:46.293 --> 00:03:47.584
taxonomy as universal.

00:03:47.808 --> 00:03:52.791
Our compact worked tree has Performance → Search
and Export; Availability → Worker loss;

00:03:52.791 --> 00:03:57.944
Maintainability → New source. The two
performance leaves make a tradeoff inside that
branch

00:03:57.944 --> 00:04:02.813
visible. Availability and Maintainability each
have one leaf in this teaching example.

00:04:02.813 --> 00:04:07.848
Rank only children of the same parent. Ranking
Availability against Performance is one

00:04:07.848 --> 00:04:13.176
conversation; ranking Search against Export is
another. Do not mix a top-level quality with

00:04:13.176 --> 00:04:18.445
a scenario several levels below it. Record the
rationale for each ordering and involve the

00:04:18.445 --> 00:04:23.539
people who bear the consequences. Check coverage
before calculating. Missing a security

00:04:23.539 --> 00:04:28.574
requirement or representing latency with many
near-duplicate scenarios can distort the

00:04:28.574 --> 00:04:29.101
decision.

00:04:29.313 --> 00:04:34.594
Mandatory requirements should be recorded
explicitly. A high weighted total cannot justify

00:04:34.594 --> 00:04:39.874
violating a requirement that stakeholders have
declared non-negotiable. Delay advocacy for

00:04:39.874 --> 00:04:44.803
particular solutions until the criteria and
priorities are established. QODA borrows

00:04:44.803 --> 00:04:50.200
scenario thinking from ATAM, but the lecture
presents it as a lightweight decision exercise,

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.313
not as a complete execution of ATAM.

00:04:52.313 --> 00:04:57.610
If Performance has ten leaves and Availability
has one, must Performance receive ten times

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:02.906
the weight? No. The top-level allocation is
determined by sibling priorities. Leaf weights

00:05:02.906 --> 00:05:08.261
subdivide their parent’s allocation. Carefully
avoid redundant leaves that double-count the

00:05:08.261 --> 00:05:09.027
same concern.

00:05:09.027 --> 00:05:16.363
Jeromy uses rank-order-centroid, abbreviated
ROC, to turn an ordered set of siblings into

00:05:16.363 --> 00:05:23.781
weights. For N children and rank k, where 1 is
highest priority, w(k) = (1/N) × Σ from i=k

00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:29.881
to N of (1/i). Each sibling set receives
positive weights that sum to one.

00:05:30.027 --> 00:05:40.416
This is a rule for translating an ordering, not
a measurement of how many times one

00:05:40.416 --> 00:05:51.682
stakeholder value exceeds another. With three
ranked qualities, w(1) = (1 + 1/2 + 1/3)/3 =

00:05:51.682 --> 00:06:02.698
11/18 ≈ 0.6111; w(2) = (1/2 + 1/3)/3 = 5/18 ≈
0.2778; and w(3) = (1/3)/3 = 1/9 ≈ 0.1111.

00:06:02.698 --> 00:06:08.123
If Performance ranks first, Availability second
and Maintainability third, assign those

00:06:08.123 --> 00:06:09.370
values respectively.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:15.749
For two siblings the weights are 0.75 and 0.25.
Thus Search above Export receives 0.75 and

00:06:15.749 --> 00:06:21.489
0.25 within Performance. A node with one child
gives it weight 1. Compute weights

00:06:21.489 --> 00:06:27.939
independently at every branching node; do not
reuse the three-child numbers for a two-child

00:06:27.939 --> 00:06:28.435
branch.

00:06:28.435 --> 00:06:34.203
The lecture uses stack rankings. If stakeholders
cannot agree on an ordering, capture the

00:06:34.203 --> 00:06:39.646
disagreement and compare alternative rankings.
Do not silently invent a tie-breaking

00:06:39.646 --> 00:06:45.414
convention or claim that the resulting decimal
values remove subjective judgment. Are the

00:06:45.414 --> 00:06:48.524
ROC weights for three siblings 0.5, 0.3 and 0.2?

00:06:48.524 --> 00:06:58.674
No. They are 11/18, 5/18 and 1/9, approximately
0.6111, 0.2778 and 0.1111. Apply the stated

00:06:58.674 --> 00:07:04.809
formula rather than substituting intuitive
percentages.

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:09.740
The combined weight of a scenario is the product
of all local weights on its root-to-leaf

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:14.614
path. Do not add the weights. The parent
allocates a share of the total, and each
descendant

00:07:14.614 --> 00:07:16.309
allocates a share of that share.

00:07:16.524 --> 00:07:31.858
Using the worked tree: Search = (11/18) × (3/4)
= 11/24 ≈ 0.4583. Export = (11/18) × (1/4) =

00:07:31.858 --> 00:07:45.692
11/72 ≈ 0.1528. Worker loss = (5/18) × 1 ≈
0.2778. New source = (1/9) × 1 ≈ 0.1111.

00:07:45.692 --> 00:07:50.871
The four leaf weights sum to one, and the two
performance leaves sum to 11/18.

00:07:50.871 --> 00:07:56.769
A deeper tree works the same way. If a
Performance → Latency branch has local weight
0.6111

00:07:56.769 --> 00:08:02.472
and a particular latency scenario has local
weight 0.75, multiply those by the top-level

00:08:02.472 --> 00:08:07.981
Performance weight as well. Omitting an
intermediate level changes the meaning of the

00:08:07.981 --> 00:08:08.694
allocation.

00:08:08.871 --> 00:08:14.167
Useful checks are local sibling sums, complete
path products and the total over all leaves.

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:19.521
If the model includes branches with no assessed
scenarios, disclose the uncovered weight. Do

00:08:19.521 --> 00:08:24.817
not silently renormalize the covered leaves and
pretend the original decision criteria were

00:08:24.817 --> 00:08:25.748
fully evaluated.

00:08:25.871 --> 00:08:33.376
Search has a 0.6111 parent weight and a 0.75
local weight. Is its total weight 1.3611? No.

00:08:33.376 --> 00:08:40.632
Multiply: approximately 0.4583. Addition would
not preserve the parent’s allocation and

00:08:40.632 --> 00:08:43.300
could produce a total above one.
